 "intro": {
  "text": "The London System is a set-up you can play against almost anything. The bishop goes to f4 before e3 so it is not shut in behind the pawns; then e3 and c3 support d4, Bd3 and Nd2 watch e4, and the king's knight heads for e5 via f3. It is popular at club level because the plans hardly change whatever Black does.",
  "credit": {
   "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5/2. Bf4",
   "url": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess_Opening_Theory/1._d4/1...d5/2._Bf4",
   "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "licenceUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
   "authors": "Wikibooks contributors (see the page history)"
  }
