     "notes": {
      "text": "2.Bf4, the Accelerated London, brings the bishop out before e3 so it will not be stuck behind your pawns, and gives simple plans against most Black set-ups. Keep an eye on b2, which the bishop no longer guards. 2.c4 (Queen's Gambit) is the main line; 2.e4?! (Blackmar-Diemer Gambit) gives up a pawn and is dubious.",
      "credit": {
       "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5",
